gpui_ios set the window's frame to the screen's bounds. iPadOS 26 runs apps in resizable windows, often smaller than the screen: the view still reported the full screen, so the app drew past its window (cut off on the right, and after rotation only partly visible) and ignored resizing. A scene's UIWindow is sized by the scene and follows it; take the initial bounds from the window.

